    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n46068" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζάθεος</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾰ], <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span></span>, also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ος</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>
		<i><span class="en">
			E.
			<u>Tr.</u>
			256
		</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
			1075
		</span></i> (lyr.); poet. Adj. (used by Trag. only in
			lyrics):—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>very
				divine, sacred</i>, of places favoured by the gods, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				1.38
			</span></i>, al. (not in <i><span class="en">
				Od.
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				<u>h.Ap.</u>
				223
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζ. Πύλος, Ἰσθμός</span>,
				<i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>P.</u>
				5.70
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>I.</u>
				1.32
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				B.
				2.7
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νᾶσος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					5.10
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πέλοπος δάπεδα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					10.24
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔναυλοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Ba.</u>
					121
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.), etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὤλενος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					284
				</span></i>
			; of things, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄνεμοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Th.</u>
					253
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χρόνος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>Pae.</u>
					6.5
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κλῇδες, σελᾶναι</span>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Tr.</u>
			</span></i>ll.cc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποταμοί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Nu.</u>
					283
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μολπαί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Ra.</u>
					385
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τιμαί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Castorio
					1
				</span></i>
			; later of persons, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀπόλλων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					9.525.7
				</span></i>
			. Adv.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-έως</span> Hdn.Gr.<i><span class="en">
				1.514
			</span></i>.</div>
